From 5c905e7164e710b9f3cb13d2a40336b7b1ac6fc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:11:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] feat(harmony): run the web app inside the HarmonyOS
 shell

The HarmonyOS app is an ArkWeb shell (paseo-harmony) around this web build.
A build with PASEO_WEB_PLATFORM=harmony resolves *.harmony.ts variants that
talk to the shell over window.paseoHarmony:

- local notifications for agent and terminal alerts, with taps routed like
  native notification responses, including taps that cold-start the app
- the background connection setting, backed by a continuous task the shell
  holds and restarts on return when the system cancelled it
- page visibility that follows the app lifecycle, so presence and the alert
  decision see Paseo leave the foreground
- shell-driven keepalive while backgrounded, since a hidden page's timers can
  be throttled below the relay's idle lease
- the back gesture: top overlay, then Back handlers, then history
- QR pairing through the system scanner, external links, system bar colours

Hover-revealed controls now stay visible whenever there is no fine pointer,
not only on native, so a touch screen in the wide layout (an unfolded
foldable, a tablet) can reach them. Native behaviour is unchanged:
useHasFinePointer is always false there.

The background connection's start and stop become awaitable, because the
shell answers asynchronously.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
